# Task

Extract the structured state established by the Story Text now and return the complete extraction.

## Rules

- Emit `new_roles` only when Cast Policy is `open` and only using the next unused candidates from New Role Candidates in rendered order; otherwise leave `new_roles` empty. Do not emit a `new_roles` entry outside Cast Policy `open`.
- Emit `role_states` only for Roles whose location, goals, or attributes actually changed; each entry must carry the complete final values and exact known `role_id`. Do not emit an unchanged Role entry.
- Emit `relationship_states` only for relationships whose trust or kind actually changed; each entry must carry the complete final values. Do not emit an unchanged relationship entry.
- Emit `add_facts`, `add_rumors`, and `add_memories` only for Knowledge the Story Text actually establishes.
- Emit `update_facts`, `update_rumors`, and `update_memories`, or `delete_rumor_ids` and `delete_memory_ids`, only for targets listed in Modifiable Knowledge. Do not mutate Knowledge outside Modifiable Knowledge.
- For every entry in Narrative Condition Queries, return exactly one `narrative_condition_judgments` entry with a matching `condition_key`, `status`, `evidence`, and `reason`. Use `unknown` when the Story Text does not settle it.
- If Validation Issues are present, resolve every one of them relative to the Previous Extraction. Do not return output identical to the Previous Extraction.
- Do not invent Role, relationship, or Knowledge state the Story Text does not establish.
- Return exactly one value matching the declared output contract. Do not return prose, explanation, planning notes, or any text outside the structured output.

# Output

Return exactly one JSON object matching the declared output contract and nothing else.
